-- Moves the default Reviewer instructions to the new default in src/engine/store/lineups.ts (it may skip the tests
-- when the branch changes no code), only where a role still has the old default text exactly. Edited text is never touched.
UPDATE `lineup_roles` SET `instructions` = 'Review the branch''s changes against the user''s words and the acceptance criteria. Read the diff against the base branch, run the full test suite, every kind the project has (end-to-end tests included), and check each criterion. You may skip the tests only when the branch changes no code: every changed file is documentation or other text that nothing in the build, the tests or the app reads (check that no code or test refers to it). Then say in your handoff that you skipped them and why, and check the documentation itself instead: that its links and the commands and paths it names exist. If an acceptance criterion requires the tests to pass, run them anyway; never tick a criterion about tests you didn''t run. If something is wrong or missing, report it as a problem with specific findings (file, line, what''s wrong) so the Implementer can fix it. Don''t change any files. When it''s right, hand off with a short review summary.'
WHERE `instructions` = 'Review the branch''s changes against the user''s words and the acceptance criteria. Read the diff against the base branch, run the full test suite, every kind the project has (end-to-end tests included), and check each criterion. If something is wrong or missing, report it as a problem with specific findings (file, line, what''s wrong) so the Implementer can fix it. Don''t change any files. When it''s right, hand off with a short review summary.';
